  Quaternions                                                                   
                                                                                
  q = q₀ + q₁i + q₂j + q₃k,  i² = j² = k² = ijk = −1 [quaternion.md]            
                                                                                
  A quaternion is a number with one real part and three imaginary parts whose   
  units satisfy i² = j² = k² = ijk = −1. A point is rotated via the sandwich    
  product v′ = qvq⁻¹, a half-turn by ½θ, with axis length √(x²+y²).             
                                                                                
  Stray dollars in prose                                                        
                                                                                
  Money like $5 and $6 must stay literal, and shell commands stay fenced:       
                                                                                
    NS=$(ip -o link show | awk -F': ' '/claude-vpn/ {print $2}')                
    ip link set $NS link up                                                     
                                                                                
  A citation [1] and an escaped paren (x) are literal punctuation (A15-1).      
  Multi-line prose where a dollar opens one line and closes the next: it costs  
  $5 and $6 across lines, still literal.                                        
